.TH UVX 1 "September 2026" "uv 0.12.17" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uvx \- run a command provided by a Python package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uvx
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uvx
runs a command provided by a Python package in an ephemeral, cached
environment, without installing it into the current project or onto the
user's path. It is an alias for \fBuv tool run\fR and ships with the same
.BR uv (1)
binary release.
.PP
By default the package name is taken to be the command name; use
\fB\-\-from\fR when they differ.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-from " FROM"
Use the given package to provide the command.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-with " \fIWITH\fR"
Run with the given packages also installed.
.TP
.BI \-\-with\-editable " WITH_EDITABLE"
Run with the given packages installed in editable mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-with\-requirements " FILE"
Run with the packages listed in the given requirements files.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-constraints " \fIFILE\fR"
Constrain versions using the given requirements files.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-build\-constraints " \fIFILE\fR"
Constrain build dependencies using the given requirements files.
.TP
.BI \-\-overrides " FILE"
Override versions using the given requirements files.
.TP
.B \-\-isolated
Run the tool in an isolated virtual environment, ignoring any
already\-installed tools.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " ENV_FILE"
Load environment variables from a \fB.env\fR file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-env\-file
Avoid reading environment variables from a \fB.env\fR file.
.TP
.BI \-\-python\-platform " PLATFORM"
The platform for which requirements should be installed.
.TP
.BI \-\-index " INDEX"
An index to use when resolving dependencies, in addition to the default
index.
.TP
.BI \-\-default\-index " DEFAULT_INDEX"
The default package index (by default, https://pypi.org/simple).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-index
Ignore the registry index, relying on direct URL dependencies and
\fB\-\-find\-links\fR instead.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-upgrade
Allow package upgrades, ignoring pinned versions.
.TP
.BI \-\-resolution " RESOLUTION"
Version selection strategy: \fBhighest\fR, \fBlowest\fR or
\fBlowest\-direct\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-reinstall
Reinstall all packages, regardless of whether they are already
installed.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-cache
Avoid reading from or writing to the cache.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Disable network access.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the concise help for this command.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the uvx version.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a linter without installing it:
.PP
.RS
.B uvx ruff check .
.RE
.PP
Run a command whose package name differs from the command:
.PP
.RS
.B uvx --from httpie http example.com
.RE
.PP
Run with an extra package available:
.PP
.RS
.B uvx --with rich python -c "import rich"
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UV_CACHE_DIR
Path to the cache directory shared with
.BR uv (1).
.TP
.B UV_PYTHON
The Python interpreter to use by default.
.TP
.B UV_ISOLATED
Run tools in an isolated environment when set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uv (1),
.BR python3 (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
